    code: 'On the naming screen at the start of the game, choose "Don\'t Care" to fill in the designers\' default names',
    effect: 'Fills in the hero\'s default name, Ness, along with default names for the rest of the party.',
    description: 'EarthBound asks the player to name the whole party, their dog and even their favourite food before the adventure begins. Choosing "Don\'t Care" fills in defaults, and the hero\'s default is Ness — a name many fans read as a nod to Nintendo\'s hardware. Every character can be renamed, but Ness became the character\'s canonical name, cemented when he appeared as a fighter in Super Smash Bros. in 1999.',
    history: 'EarthBound was released in Japan on 27 August 1994 as Mother 2 and in North America on 5 June 1995. It was developed by Ape and HAL Laboratory, written and directed by Shigesato Itoi, and produced by Satoru Iwata, later Nintendo\'s president. Itoi wanted characters players could recognise in people they knew, and Ness is a 13-year-old from the town of Onett who fights with a baseball bat and a yo-yo.\n\nNintendo spent about $2 million on a North American campaign that sardonically declared "This game stinks", complete with scratch-and-sniff advertisements, but the game sold only about 140,000 copies in the US. Its reputation grew afterwards, helped by Ness\'s place in Super Smash Bros. — he was nearly replaced by Lucas in Melee, until Mother 3\'s Nintendo 64 release was cancelled — and EarthBound returned on the Wii U Virtual Console in 2013 and the SNES Classic in 2017.',
    type: 'Hidden Feature',
