    history: 'GoldenEye 007 was developed by Rare and published by Nintendo, directed and produced by Martin Hollis. Work began in January 1995 and took about two and a half years; the project was first conceived as a 2D platformer for the Super NES. It was released in Japan on 23 August 1997 and in North America two days later.\n\nIt offered four-player split-screen deathmatch, and it sold more than eight million copies, the third-best-selling Nintendo 64 game. It scored 96 on Metacritic and won a BAFTA Interactive Entertainment Award and four AIAS awards. The time targets that unlock its cheats doubled as challenges for players, and a speedrun community has been active around the game since at least 1999.',
