    description: 'The original Tomb Raider on PlayStation hides its cheats in the inventory screen: with the inventory open, a sequence of shoulder and face buttons gives Lara every weapon and full ammunition, and a second sequence skips to the next level. The button order differs between the North American and PAL releases. There is also a route without codes: finish the game, then start a new one without quitting. The better-known cheat performed by walking, turning and back-flipping — including the variant that makes Lara explode — belongs to Tomb Raider II, not this game.',
    history: 'Tomb Raider was developed by Core Design, with Toby Gard as lead artist and Lara Croft\'s creator, and published by Eidos Interactive. The Sega Saturn version came first, in Europe on 24 October 1996, followed by the PlayStation and MS-DOS versions in North America on 14 November. It sold more than seven million copies, topped the British charts a record three times, and remained the series\' best-selling game until the 2013 reboot.\n\nLara\'s popularity produced a persistent rumour that a cheat would make her appear nude. According to the developers, management did suggest one, and the team refused. A fan-made "Nude Raider" patch for the PC version did circulate, and Eidos sent cease-and-desist letters to sites hosting it; the secret code in Tomb Raider II that was rumoured to be the nude cheat in fact makes Lara explode.',
